 world is  full of it if I can convert it to  visible power he says to large views of  War will be erased from the world and  back to Tesla that idea of using  invisible energy all around us and  making it visible through electricity  and stuff like wireless light bulbs  definitely makes me think that Oda got  some of this stuff from Tesla himself  who everyone said was way ahead of his  time vegapunk says surely science will  reach that point one day although part  of me still thinks people will find  reasons to have War besides Energy but  at least they'll have less reasons  anyways as vegapunks proclaiming his  dream we get an absolutely amazing panel  making him look like he's Heaven Sent I  absolutely love the setup of this pen  and it's a very nice idea to that  vegapunk has especially since science  can often lead to worse damage during  Wars because of Advanced Technology  being able to cause more damage with  less effort he's definitely an idealist  and I'm glad he's not just an amoral  scientist who doesn't care what happens  as long as he progresses science I like  that his goals piece and it makes sense  that he gets along with the also peace  driven Dragon also I'm definitely seeing  the Albert Einstein similarities in some  of these panels look wise the idea is  like I said mostly remind me of Tesla  but look wise definitely Vega bunker  mines with Albert Einstein and I love  how Oda draws from everything for  inspiration including fiction and  non-fiction nothing is off limits Lu  Luffy for his part doesn't seem moved he  explains that he thinks a person that  can make everyone happy is good but he's  not interested in being a hero though  and it's funny that he keeps saying this  while continuing to act rather  heroically in situations like wano where  he wants to help and protect the people  it makes him all the more likable though  because he does the good stuff but is  not conceited or on a high horse about  it and it also gives him the rebel  appeal that pirates should have which  makes me love him all the more megapunt  goes on to explain that he's seeking the  energy that Dynamic power source that  was able to power the ancient robot  Soldier he's gotten close to finding out  about that ancient energy he wonders if  he unravels the strings of the Forbidden  history what on Earth will he be able to  comprehend he says in the course of  inheriting his friend's will he is  quickly getting close to the truth and  just then bam an explosion happens which  of course is cp0 getting closer Vega  Punk realizes that he's running a of  time so he concludes that in short he  stepped too deep into the Forbidden  story so he will be eliminated by the  world government just like what they did  to Ohara I really like how in this way  Oda Hypes up the importance of knowledge  and history so much to the point where  people will do anything to stop you from  figuring it out and of course it makes  the mystery all the more intense and  intriguing it's explained to Luffy that  cp0 those who act only under orders of  the celestial dragons and that they are  at the top of cyberpole I'm really  excited to see an old villain that Luffy  beat up pop up again and stay relevant  that's another thing I love about one  piece how the villains can continue to  grow strengthwise along with the  protagonist and that definitely goes for  Blackbeard too however I still don't see  Rob Lucci being able to beat yonko Luffy  so I'm interested in seeing where Oda  plans to take this not surprisingly  Usopp is freaking out when they realize  that Rob Luchi and the rest made it  inside Rob was right about the Sea Beast  destroying their ship so it looks like  this has to come to a head I'm excited  to see Punk one AKA Daft Punk as I like  to call him preparing to release  seraphim s snake s hock and S shark for  battle considering what we've seen from  them so far I feel like cp0 shouldn't be  able to just Breeze through these next  level pacifist